{
  "_comment": "Fonts the looks draw text with. python tools/make_font.py --profile s3 turns each entry into src/looks/fonts/s3/<name>.h (anti-aliased glyph tables, sized in pixels on the 240 px dial). Variable fonts take a weight (wght); skew leans the glyphs right by that many degrees. 'profiles' names the resolutions one display class ships: 1 is the design size the looks are laid out at, and the rest are the real pixels per design pixel on its screens (240 -> 1x, 320 -> 1.3333x, 412 -> 1.7167x, 466 -> 1.9417x). Every profile starts at 1.0: layout and ascent are defined in design pixels. A new board either uses an existing profile or adds one and regenerates; the build asserts that the selected profile covers the board's scale (see src/main.cpp). s3 (firmware) and all (simulator) are committed profiles; p4-720 is generated when its board is added.",
